data.projectDigest:
To fully embrace cybersecurity as an enabler of economic stability and development, countries are strongly dependent on the availability of local capacities, among which knowledge, skills and services are prominent. Building local cybersecurity capabilities is a long-term endeavor to address structural shortcomings in a sustainable manner. But many capacity building efforts are currently deployed in silos, either by stakeholder or sector. A lack of coordination between relevant actors, the cybersecurity skills gap and market fragmentation are barriers to cybersecurity at local and international level as well.

By supporting the creation and acceleration of local cybersecurity ecosystems and their connection in a global network, the project aims at fostering a pragmatic and inclusive multi-stakeholder approach to building cyber capabilities, that will result in: a) more extensive knowledge (from leaders to global public) and b) effective integration of public institutions and business strategies to support local market development, innovation and wealth creation.

The Cybersecurity Ecosystems Project will result in:

· Increased leadership (including leaders in public, private, policy and tech spheres, across local and global dimensions) awareness and commitment on building cyber capabilities;

· Improved leadership in understanding priority areas and initiatives (new or existing) for action, public-private cooperation and resourcing;

· Enhanced global cooperation on improving cyber capabilities between emerged and emerging economies.

